 "identification_note": "Observational: customers' order histories and their returns share unobserved causes (business size, assortment fit); feature effects are associations.",
 "extrapolation_limits": "UCI Online Retail II: 5,942 customers of one UK online gift-ware retailer (many of them wholesalers), 2009-12-01..2011-12-09. The simulator may use this model for the probability that a customer who bought from a shop today buys from the same shop again within 90 days, given its order history (frequency, recency, tenure, spend, basket breadth, returns). It may NOT infer: (1) retention for subscriptions, digital products or consumers of other shops (one retailer, mostly business customers); (2) responses to price, service quality or marketing (not features; observational); (3) horizons other than 90 days; (4) behaviour after 2011 or outside the UK-centred customer base; lines without a customer id (23%) are excluded, so guest buyers are not represented.",
